# Chroma library, modern Earth: JUVENILE stage (ages 10 to 18). Grid: earth-plan.md. Rules: library-spec.md.
# Syntax: header of build.py. Compile and check the whole batch: python3 build.py earth

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- pair 1: calls WU (cycle s2) / calls BRG (cycle s4)

== exams are coming
tier: everyday
at: school
stages: juvenile
age: 13-18
calls: WU
tone: trouble
life: school
horizon: week
roles: parent, rival, friend, a teacher
earth: the big end-of-year exams are three weeks away and revision has barely started
times: Nearly every teenager in school, once or twice a year, before the big end-of-year exams (estimate)
gap: .8-1
scene: The exams start in three weeks. {Ns} desk is buried under past papers, and the phone keeps lighting up.
scene W: The exam timetable is stuck to the fridge, every date circled in pen by {parent}. {N} means to be ready for each one.
scene U: {N} spreads the whole syllabus across the floor. There are gaps in it, and gaps can be mapped and filled.
scene B: Only the top marks get a place in the advanced class next year, and {rival} has been revising since the spring.
scene R: The sun is out, the exams are weeks away, and every hour at the desk feels like a cage.
scene G: {N} has always been good at some subjects and hopeless at others, like {parent} before them. Three weeks will not change that much.
- W | revise every evening at the same time, with the phone in another room | habit | v: conformity, achievement | chance: 78
- U | work through every past paper and study each mistake you make | habit | v: achievement, self-direction | mark: learned a skill | chance: 82
- B | get hold of the answers going round the group chats | habit | v: achievement | mark: hid a wrong | closed: approval: cheating; backfire: caught, and the paper voided | tech: phone | chance: 30
- R | turn revision into a loud game with friends: quizzes, forfeits, music | habit | v: hedonism | chance: 60
- G | keep your usual days, sleep and meals, and trust what you already know | v: security | chance: 48
- W>B | sign up for every extra revision class, to finish ahead of your rival | v: achievement | chance: 62
- U>R | plan revision so cleverly that your evenings stay free | v: hedonism, self-direction | chance: 62
- B>G | drop the subjects you will fail anyway, and pour everything into your gifts | v: achievement | mark: took a wild risk | chance: 59
- R>W | pull all-nighters before each paper, so you do not let the family down | body: light | v: conformity, achievement | chance: 45
- G>U | learn it all by heart the old-fashioned way, reading your notes aloud until they stick | habit | v: tradition, achievement | chance: 65
works: The paper turns over, and the first question is one {N} knows cold.
works: The results come in, better than {N} dared to hope.
fails: {Ns} mind goes blank halfway through the first paper.
fails: The results arrive, and {parent} goes very quiet.

== a fight after school
tier: everyday
at: school
stages: juvenile
age: 11-17
calls: BRG
tone: trouble
life: conflict, body
horizon: moment
roles: rival, friend, a teacher, a crowd of onlookers
earth: word goes round that someone is going to fight you at the gates after school
times: About 1 in 3 teenagers, once or twice; about 1 in 4 US high school boys and 1 in 8 girls are in a physical fight in a year (CDC YRBS 2021)
gap: 2-4
share: .33
rate: 1
# rate lowered (drafts/repeats/everyday.py)
scene: Word has gone round: {rival} will be waiting at the gates after the last bell, and half the year is coming to watch.
scene W: {N} has done nothing to deserve this, and everyone knows it. Somebody ought to stop it before it starts.
scene U: {N} replays the last week, trying to work out what {rival} thinks happened and who stirred it up.
scene B: If {N} backs down now, the whole school will know by morning. This is about who gets pushed around for the next three years.
scene R: {Ns} heart is hammering and their fists are already tight. The last lesson drags on for ever.
scene G: Some fights come whatever anyone does. {N} feels this one in the stomach, the way a dog feels a storm on the way.
- W | tell the teacher on gate duty what is planned | v: security, conformity | closed: approval: telling on others; backfire: called a snitch for the rest of the year | chance: 75
- U | message your rival first and find out what they think you did | v: security | act: message their rival first and find out what the rival thinks they did | tech: phone | chance: 55
- B | get two older kids to stand behind you at the gate | v: power, security | act: get two older kids to stand behind them at the gate | chance: 72
- R | walk out of the gate past them, head up, and refuse to fight | v: self-direction | chance: 60
- G | round up your cousins and the kids from your street to face them together | identity | body: heavy | v: benevolence (in-group), power | closed: approval: a gang fight; backfire: everyone suspended, and a feud between streets | chance: 50
- W>G | ask your parents to ring the other family and settle it between the households | v: security, tradition | chance: 52
- U>W | save the threatening messages and hand them to the head of year | v: security, conformity | tech: phone | chance: 75
- B>U | pay one of their friends to tell you exactly what is planned | v: security, power | act: pay one of their friends to tell them exactly what is planned | chance: 54
- R>B | throw the first punch, so nobody pushes you around again | body: heavy | v: power | mark: made an enemy | closed: approval: fighting; backfire: suspended, and the feud goes on | act: throw the first punch, so nobody pushes them around again | role: men | chance: 50
- G>R | have it out fair and square on the field, then shake hands and let it go | body: heavy | v: none clear (settling it by strength) | mark: took a wild risk | closed: approval: fighting; backfire: caught by a teacher, and both suspended | role: men | chance: 45
works: It is over almost before it starts, and by Friday nobody is talking about it.
works: {N} walks home with friends, and {rival} keeps well away.
fails: There is a scuffle at the gates, a torn shirt, and a letter home.
fails: The next day everyone is talking about {N}, and not kindly.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- pair 2: calls UB (cycle s3) / calls WRG (cycle s1)

== you learn a secret about a friend
tier: everyday
stages: juvenile
age: 12-18
calls: UB
tone: mixed
life: friends
horizon: week
roles: friend, rival, the group
earth: you find out your friend is secretly going out with someone the whole group can't stand
times: Most teenagers, about once a year (estimate)
gap: .8-1
scene: A message lights up {friend}'s phone, and {N} sees the name: {rival}. {friend} has been going out with them in secret for weeks.
scene W: The group swore there would be no secrets between them. {N} cannot decide which matters more, the promise or the friend.
scene U: So that explains the late replies and the strange excuses. {N} starts fitting the rest of it together.
scene B: Nobody else knows. For once {N} holds something the whole group would give a lot to hear.
scene R: It lands like a slap: {friend}, of all people, and with {rival}.
scene G: People fall for whoever they fall for. {N} watches {friend} smile at the phone and remembers how long the two of them have been friends.
- W | tell your friend you will not lie for them, and that secrets break the group | v: benevolence (honesty), conformity | chance: 60
- U | read back through their messages while they are out of the room | v: self-direction | mark: hid a wrong | closed: approval: reading a friend's phone; backfire: caught, and the friendship ends | act: read back through their friend's messages while the friend is out of the room | tech: phone | chance: 62
- B | keep the secret, and make sure your friend knows you are keeping it | v: power | chance: 80
- R | blurt it out at lunch in front of everyone | v: stimulation | mark: made an enemy | chance: 12
- G | let it be; it is their life, and the friendship matters more | v: benevolence, universalism (tolerance) | chance: 80
- W>R | swear to keep their secret, and cover for them when they sneak off | binds | v: benevolence | mark: hid a wrong | closed: approval: lying to parents for a friend; backfire: caught in the lie, and both in trouble | chance: 70
- U>G | spend time with the one the group can't stand, to see what your friend sees | door | identity | v: universalism (tolerance) | mark: made a friend | chance: 60
- B>W | use what you know to force a truce between your group and theirs | v: security, power | chance: 32
- R>U | ask them straight out, right now, how on earth it happened | v: self-direction | chance: 80
- G>B | wait it out patiently; when it ends, your friend will owe you | v: power | act: wait it out patiently; when it ends, their friend will owe them | chance: 65
works: The secret stays where it belongs, and the friendship holds.
works: {friend} tells the others in their own time, and it goes better than anyone feared.
fails: By Monday everyone knows, and {friend} thinks {N} told them.
fails: {friend} stops answering {Ns} messages.

== summer camp
tier: everyday
stages: juvenile
age: 10-16
calls: WRG
tone: joy
life: leisure, nature
horizon: week
roles: friend, a counsellor, the other campers
earth: two weeks at a summer camp by a lake, sleeping in cabins, phones handed in at the gate
times: About 1 in 3 young people, one or a few summers, at a camp or on a school residential trip (estimate)
gap: .8-1
share: .33
rate: 1
# rate lowered (drafts/repeats/everyday.py)
scene: The coach pulls up at a camp by a lake. Phones go into a basket at the gate, and the cabins smell of pine and old sleeping bags.
scene W: There is a washing-up rota, a flag raised every morning, and points for the tidiest cabin. {N} wants their cabin to win.
scene U: The lake, the woods, a night sky with no streetlights: {N} has a notebook and two weeks to find out about all of it.
scene B: The cabins choose their leaders on the first night. {N} quietly sizes up who the others will listen to.
scene R: No parents, no phones, and a rope swing over the water. {N} drops their bag and runs.
scene G: The air smells of pine and woodsmoke, and by the second night {N} sleeps better than they have all year.
- W | look out for the shy kid in your cabin and bring them into every game | v: benevolence | mark: made a friend | chance: 82
- U | spend your free hours at the nature hut, identifying everything you find | v: self-direction | chance: 88
- B | trade the snacks from home for the best bunk and the easiest chores | v: power, hedonism | chance: 88
- R | try the rope swing, the climbing wall and the kayaks, all on the first day | body: heavy | v: stimulation | chance: 92
- G | let go of home and phones, and live by the sun and the lake | door | v: universalism (nature), hedonism | chance: 72
- W>U | go to every workshop on the timetable and earn every badge | v: achievement | mark: learned a skill | chance: 60
- U>B | find a loophole in the camp's points system and win your cabin the trophy | v: achievement, power | closed: approval: gaming the rules; backfire: the points struck off on the last day | chance: 32
- B>R | sneak into the kitchen after lights out and raid the sweets | v: hedonism | mark: defied an authority | closed: approval: out of bounds at night; backfire: caught, and no campfire on the last night | chance: 65
- R>G | leap into the cold lake at dawn with the whole cabin, whooping | body: heavy | v: stimulation | chance: 90
- G>W | comfort the homesick younger ones at bedtime with the stories you grew up with | v: benevolence, tradition | mark: helped someone in need | chance: 82
works: {N} comes home sunburnt and scratched, with three new friends and a song stuck in their head.
works: On the last night, round the fire, {N} does not want it to end.
fails: {N} is homesick from the first night and counts the days.
fails: A row in the cabin sours the whole fortnight.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- pair 3: calls BR (cycle s4) / calls WUG (cycle s2)

== a party at a house with no parents
tier: everyday
stages: juvenile
age: 13-18
calls: BR
tone: joy
life: friends, leisure
horizon: moment
roles: friend, rival, parent, the host, a neighbour
earth: an older kid's parents are away for the weekend, and half the year is invited round
times: Most teenagers, once or a few times, mostly between fifteen and eighteen (estimate)
gap: .8-1
scene: The parents are away, the house is packed by nine, and the music shakes the windows. Somebody has brought bottles from home.
scene W: {N} promised {parent} to be home by eleven. The kitchen is already a mess, and the neighbours have started looking out of their windows.
scene U: {N} leans against the wall for a while, watching who talks to whom and working out how the night is going to go.
scene B: Everyone who matters in the year is here. A night like this decides who is in and who is out.
scene R: The bass is in {Ns} chest, everyone is shouting the words, and the night has only just begun.
scene G: Half the faces here {N} has known since they were small. Out in the garden it is cool and quiet, and the stars are out.
- W | phone the host's parents when things get out of hand | identity | v: security, conformity | mark: made an enemy | closed: approval: telling on the party; backfire: frozen out by half the year | chance: 45
- U | nurse one drink all night and watch how everyone else behaves | v: security, self-direction | closed: law: underage drinking; backfire: caught along with everyone else | law: alcohol | chance: 92
- B | take a bottle from your parents' cabinet to get in with the right crowd | habit | v: power | mark: hid a wrong | closed: law: underage drinking, and the bottle is not theirs to take; backfire: found out at home | law: alcohol | chance: 72
- R | drink, dance, and stay until the very end | habit | body: light | v: hedonism, stimulation | closed: law: underage drinking; backfire: sick, caught, and grounded | law: alcohol | chance: 75
- G | keep to the garden with your oldest friends, and freeze out the newcomers | v: security | mark: made an enemy | closed: approval: freezing people out; backfire: the host asks the whole crowd to leave | chance: 65
- W>G | stay behind and help the host clean up before the parents get back | v: benevolence, conformity | mark: hid a wrong | closed: approval: covering up the party; backfire: the parents find out anyway, and the helpers get the blame | chance: 60
- U>W | plan the lifts and the night buses so everyone gets home safe | v: security, benevolence | chance: 75
- B>U | work the room and collect everyone's gossip to use later | v: power | chance: 92
- R>B | challenge the most popular kid to a drinking game, and win | body: light | v: power, stimulation | mark: took a wild risk | closed: law: underage drinking; backfire: sick in front of everyone | law: alcohol | chance: 42
- G>R | put on the old songs everyone knows and get the whole house singing | v: hedonism | chance: 62
works: It is the best night of the year, and the photos prove it.
works: {N} gets home on time, tired and happy, with a story to tell.
fails: A neighbour calls the police about the noise, and every parent hears about it.
fails: {N} wakes up with a pounding head and a phone full of messages they would rather not read.

== a Saturday job at the corner shop
tier: everyday
at: employer
stages: juvenile
age: 13-18
calls: WUG
tone: mixed
life: work, money
horizon: week
roles: boss, friend, a regular customer, the owner's family
earth: your first part-time job, Saturdays at the corner shop, and today the owner leaves you alone at the till
times: About half of teenagers, once, a first part-time job while at school; about 15 in 100 teenagers a year start one (estimate)
once: yes
share: .5
rate: 1
# rate lowered (drafts/repeats/everyday.py)
scene: It is {Ns} third Saturday at the corner shop, and today {boss} has gone to the wholesaler and left {N} alone behind the till.
scene W: {boss} counted the float with {N} this morning and handed over the keys. {N} means to account for every penny.
scene U: The stockroom is chaos, the price labels are a mess, and {N} can already see three ways to run the place better.
scene B: A till full of cash, shelves of cigarettes and scratch cards, and nobody watching. {N} notices all of it.
scene R: The sun is out, {friend} keeps texting from the park, and {N} is stuck stacking tins.
scene G: The same faces come in every Saturday: the old man for his paper, the twins for sweets. {N} is starting to know them all by name.
- W | count the till to the penny and write down every sale | habit | v: conformity, benevolence (dependability) | chance: 92
- U | learn the stock system and sort out the chaos in the stockroom | v: achievement, self-direction | mark: learned a skill | chance: 75
- B | pocket a few notes from the till; the owner never counts properly | habit | v: power, hedonism | mark: hid a wrong | closed: law: theft; backfire: caught on the camera, and sacked | chance: 70
- R | turn the radio up and dance behind the counter between customers | v: hedonism | chance: 92
- G | chat with the regulars and learn everyone's name and usual order | habit | v: benevolence | mark: made a friend | chance: 85
- W>B | follow every rule so well that the owner gives you more hours | v: achievement | act: follow every rule so well that the owner gives them more hours | chance: 55
- U>R | learn the routine so well you finish early and have the shop to yourself | v: hedonism, self-direction | chance: 72
- B>G | slip the out-of-date food to the old man who can't afford his shopping | v: benevolence | mark: helped someone in need | closed: approval: giving away stock; backfire: the owner docks the pay | chance: 90
- R>W | run after the kid who just pocketed a drink and bring it back | body: heavy | v: security, conformity | chance: 62
- G>U | ask the owner's mother, who ran the shop for forty years, how she did it | v: tradition, self-direction | chance: 90
works: {boss} comes back, checks the till, and asks {N} to do Sundays as well.
works: At five o'clock {N} walks out with a pay packet and a story for {friend}.
fails: The till is short at closing, and {N} cannot explain it.
fails: {boss} comes back early, at the worst possible moment.

