== a band or a sport that takes over your life
tier: everyday
stages: juvenile
age: 12-18
calls: RG
tone: joy
life: passion, body
horizon: months
roles: mentor, friend, parent, the band or the team
earth: the band you started with friends, or the club you joined, now fills every evening and weekend
times: About 1 in 3 teenagers, one or two such passions in the teenage years (estimate)
gap: 2-4
share: .33
rate: 1
# rate lowered (drafts/repeats/everyday.py)
scene: These days {Ns} life runs on one thing: practice after school, again at weekends, and the rest of the time thinking about it.
scene W: {mentor} expects everyone at every session, on time and ready. {N} has not missed one since the autumn.
scene U: {N} films every session and watches it back at night, looking for the one thing to fix next.
scene B: There is talk of a scout coming, or a real gig in front of a real crowd. {N} intends to be the one people remember.
scene R: When it is going well, nothing else exists: no homework, no worries, just sweat and noise and joy.
scene G: {N} found this the way a seedling finds the light. It feels less like a hobby than something they were born to do.
- W | never miss a session, and be the one who sets up and packs away | habit | v: benevolence (dependability), conformity | chance: 76
- U | study the best in the world and drill your weakest skill | habit | v: achievement | mark: learned a skill | self_control: + | chance: 76
- B | put in the extra hours to earn the lead spot outright | habit | identity | v: achievement, power | mark: learned a skill | self_control: + | chance: 60
- R | let it swallow everything else: homework, sleep, the lot | habit | v: stimulation, hedonism | chance: 68
- G | play by feel, the way it comes most naturally | v: self-direction | chance: 62
- W>U | sign up for proper lessons or coaching and do every exercise they set | v: achievement | mark: learned a skill | chance: 72
- U>B | work out what the scouts or the bookers look for, and give them exactly that | v: achievement, power | chance: 35
- B>R | talk the head into letting you off lessons on match or gig days | v: self-direction | act: talk the head into letting them off lessons on match or gig days | chance: 42
- R>G | throw yourself in so hard that the others become your second family | binds | v: benevolence | chance: 85
- G>W | stay loyal to the club or band that took you in, whoever else calls | binds | v: tradition, benevolence | act: stay loyal to the club or band that took them in, whoever else calls | chance: 65
works: The big day comes, and {N} is better than they have ever been.
works: Someone who matters says {Ns} name out loud.
fails: {Ns} grades slide, and {parent} sets a deadline: fix them, or give it up.
fails: An injury, a row, a split: in one week it is over, for now.

== a group project where nobody pulls their weight
tier: everyday
at: school
stages: juvenile
age: 11-18
calls: WUB
tone: trouble
life: school
horizon: week
roles: friend, rival, a teacher, classmates
earth: a group project counts for a big mark, and the rest of your group is doing nothing
times: Most students, about once a year or more (estimate)
gap: .8-1
scene: The group project is due on Friday. In the group chat {N} has asked four times who is doing what, and nobody has answered.
scene W: The task sheet says every member must contribute. {N} reads it again and wonders whose job it is to make that true.
scene U: {N} can see exactly how the project should go. The problem is the three people who are meant to help.
scene B: Everyone gets the same mark, whoever does the work. {N} thinks hard about who should get the credit.
scene R: {N} wants to shake every one of them. Friday is four days away and the slides are still blank.
scene G: It is always this way: some pull and some drift, like any herd. {N} has always been one of the ones who pull.
- W | split the work fairly, write down who does what, and chase them up | v: conformity | chance: 55
- U | do the whole thing yourself, and do it properly | identity | v: achievement | chance: 75
- B | do the key part yourself, and hold it back until they do theirs | v: power, achievement | chance: 65
- R | blow up at them all in the group chat | v: none clear (frustration let out) | tech: phone | chance: 40
- G | do your own part, let the rest go, and accept whatever mark comes | v: tradition (humility) | chance: 35
- W>R | report the slackers to the teacher by name, and ask to work alone next time | v: self-direction, conformity | closed: approval: telling on classmates; backfire: frozen out by the group | chance: 58
- U>G | find what each of them is actually good at and give them that part | v: benevolence, achievement | chance: 65
- B>W | promise pizza if they all come round and do their share | v: conformity | chance: 78
- R>U | pitch a wild new idea that gets everyone fired up to work | v: stimulation, self-direction | chance: 58
- G>B | let the slackers sink, and make your own part the one that stands out | v: achievement, power | chance: 55
works: The project comes back with the top mark, and the teacher mentions {Ns} part by name.
works: Against all odds, the group pulls together on the last night.
fails: The presentation falls apart in front of the whole class.
fails: Everyone gets the same poor mark, and {N} fumes about it for weeks.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- pair 5: calls WG (cycle s2) / calls UBR (cycle s4)

== a coming-of-age ceremony
tier: everyday
at: faith body
stages: juvenile
age: 12-16
calls: WG
tone: joy
life: faith, tradition
horizon: months
rite: young_adult
roles: parent, grandparent, elder, a priest or teacher of the faith
earth: your confirmation, bar or bat mitzvah, or another coming-of-age rite is set for the spring, with classes first
times: Under half of teenagers in most rich countries now, once, at twelve to sixteen; more where the family keeps a faith (estimate)
