- U | ask the hard questions, and go through with it only if the answers hold | v: self-direction | chance: 55
- B | go through with it for the party, the presents and the envelopes of money | v: hedonism, power | chance: 90
- R | tell your parents you don't believe it, and will not stand up and pretend | identity | v: self-direction | mark: defied an authority | chance: 45
- G | wear the old family clothes and do it exactly as your family always has | identity | v: tradition | tags: commit:faith | chance: 85
- W>B | deliver your reading perfectly, so it outshines your cousin's last year | v: achievement | chance: 45
- U>R | study the faith deeply and make it your own, on your own terms | identity | v: self-direction | tags: commit:faith | chance: 72
- B>G | strike a deal: you will do it for a trip to where your grandparents grew up | binds | v: tradition, power | tags: commit:faith | chance: 64
- R>W | stand up and speak the vow with your whole heart, voice shaking | binds | v: tradition | tags: commit:faith | chance: 85
- G>U | ask your grandparents what the old words meant to them, and write it all down | v: tradition, self-direction | chance: 92
works: The day goes beautifully, and {parent} cries in the front row.
works: {N} walks out of the ceremony feeling taller, and older.
fails: {N} stumbles over the words in front of everyone.
fails: The day turns into a family row, and nobody remembers the ceremony.

== someone starts mocking you online
tier: everyday
stages: juvenile
age: 11-18
calls: UBR
tone: trouble
life: friends, media
horizon: week
roles: rival, friend, parent, a teacher
earth: an account nobody admits to has started posting memes that make fun of you
times: Many teenagers, once or twice; about 1 in 6 US high school students are bullied online in a year (CDC YRBS 2023)
gap: 2-4
rate: 1
# rate lowered (drafts/repeats/everyday.py)
scene: An account with no name has started posting memes about {N}: the clothes, the voice, the walk. By lunchtime half the year has seen them.
scene W: There are rules about this at school, and laws outside it. {N} wonders why nobody has stopped it yet.
scene U: Whoever runs the account writes like someone {N} knows. The spelling, the timing, the jokes: it is a puzzle, and puzzles can be solved.
scene B: Someone thinks they can make {N} small. {N} starts thinking about what that someone has to lose.
scene R: Every new post makes {Ns} face burn. {N} wants to scream, throw the phone, find whoever it is.
scene G: {N} puts the phone face down and goes out into the garden. The trees do not care what anyone posts.
- W | report the account, and ask the school to deal with it | v: conformity, security | chance: 45
- U | hack into the account to find out who runs it | v: security, self-direction | closed: law: getting into someone's account; backfire: traced, and in trouble with the police | chance: 15
- B | dig up something on whoever is behind it, and let them know you have it | v: power | mark: made an enemy | chance: 30
- R | post a video laughing at the memes yourself, so they lose their sting | v: none clear (laughing it off) | chance: 50
- G | log off for a week and spend it with people who know you | v: security, benevolence | act: log off for a week and spend it with people who know them | chance: 45
- W>G | tell your parents everything, and let the family close ranks around you | v: security | act: tell their parents everything, and let the family close ranks around them | chance: 55
- U>W | trace the account to its owner and take the proof to their parents | v: security, conformity | mark: made an enemy | chance: 55
- B>U | make a fake account to get inside their circle and find out who it is | v: security | closed: approval: lying online; backfire: found out, and the mockery gets worse | chance: 50
- R>B | confront the one you suspect in the corridor, so everyone sees you are not scared | v: power | chance: 60
